.claude/commands/.wrap-init.json

# playwright-bdd generated tests + reports (apps/admin, #595)
.features-gen/

# Codex skill bridge — CONTENTS only (#1261). `.agents/skills` itself is TRACKED
# (a symlink blob; `pnpm agent:setup` materialises it as a Windows junction onto
# `apps/docs/content/skills/`). Without this rule git-for-Windows descends INTO the
# junction: `git add -A` stages ~28 phantom paths under `.agents/skills/**`, and any
# routine unwind of that add (`git reset --hard`, `git stash`, `git checkout -- .`)
# then removes those phantom paths THROUGH the junction — deleting the REAL skill
# catalog, the AGENTS.md §3.3 contract surface. Ignoring the subtree makes git blind
# to it, so nothing can be staged (or unstaged) through the link. No-op on POSIX,
# where the bridge is a real symlink git never traverses.
/.agents/skills/**
